Run benchmark questions as retriever + LLM backend: the retriever finds chunks, the LLM answers.

  --retriever  none | gemini_file_search | vertex_rag_engine | langchain_vector | graphrag_local | ragflow
               (systems/retrievers.py; graphrag_local runs in the graphrag environment)
  --llm        a backend in pipeline/llm_backends.json        (pipeline/llm_backends.py)

A profile with messages(q, contexts) gives the request itself (EnterpriseRAG-Bench: the
official answer prompt in one user message). Otherwise the system message is the profile's
SYSTEM_PROMPT and the user message has the chunks under "---Knowledge Base---" (the layout of
the GraphRAG-Bench LightRAG prompt) and then the question; with --retriever none it is the
question only. The IDs of the retrieved documents go to the prediction when the retriever
returns them (document_ids). The chunks are stored as
`context`. Retrieval and generation are retried separately, and their latency, tokens and
cost are recorded separately (extra.retrieval_s, extra.generation_s). A stopped run continues
where it stopped (runs.jsonl).

    ./bench graphrag-bench pilot_gptoss_norag eval systems/run_rag.py --subset medical \
        --llm bedrock-gpt-oss-120b --retriever none \
        --questions-file data/Questions/pilot_questions.json --out-dir runs/<YYYY-MM-DD>_<name>/gptoss_norag

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --subset {all}        EnterpriseRAG-Bench subset to process
  --questions-file QUESTIONS_FILE
                        a question file in the official format (default: the
                        full subset)
  --sample SAMPLE       first N questions of each source (0 = all)
  --full                run the full question set (only when the operator has
                        approved a full run)
  --workers WORKERS
  --max-attempts MAX_ATTEMPTS
  --backoff BACKOFF     first retry wait in seconds; doubles each time
  --timeout TIMEOUT
  --out-dir OUT_DIR     for a comparison: runs/<YYYY-MM-DD>_<name>/<system>
  --dry-run             print the first request and stop
  --llm {anthropic-claude-haiku-5-5,anthropic-claude-haiku-5-5-nothink,bedrock-gpt-oss-120b,gemini-3.8-flash,openai-gpt-4o-mini,openai-gpt-5-mini,openai-gpt-5.4,openai-text-embedding-3-large}
  --retriever {none,gemini_file_search,vertex_rag_engine,langchain_vector,graphrag_local,ragflow}
  --top-k TOP_K         chunks per search (reference runner: 5)
  --store STORE         gemini_file_search: the File Search store
  --retrieval-model RETRIEVAL_MODEL
                        gemini_file_search: the Gemini model that makes the
                        search
  --retrieval-instruction {cite_each,official}
                        gemini_file_search: system instruction of the search
                        call (see RETRIEVAL_INSTRUCTIONS)
  --rag-setup RAG_SETUP
                        vertex_rag_engine: setup.json from setup_rag_engine.py
  --chunk-limit CHUNK_LIMIT
                        langchain_vector: chunks to fetch before deduplication
                        to --top-k documents
  --langchain-index LANGCHAIN_INDEX
                        langchain_vector: the folder from setup_langchain.py
  --graphrag-index GRAPHRAG_INDEX
                        graphrag_local: the folder from setup_graphrag.py
  --community-level COMMUNITY_LEVEL
                        graphrag_local: community level of the reports
                        (GraphRAG CLI default: 2)
  --ragflow-setup RAGFLOW_SETUP
                        ragflow: setup.json from setup_ragflow.py
  --ragflow-top-n RAGFLOW_TOP_N
                        ragflow: chunks per search (top_n of a default RAGFlow
                        chat assistant: 6)

